From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: thecorporatetractor <marco@azarguard.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 17:41:32 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 07/16] lokql: --quiet startup; .save writes empty results and
 refuses failed ones

- --quiet (run, explore, convert): only errors are printed while the data
  files, commands and scripts given on the command line run; explore turns
  output back on at the prompt. Loading a dataset no longer floods the
  screen, and scripted runs print nothing but errors.
- .save of an empty result writes an empty file (JSON [] or a CSV header)
  instead of warning 'No rows to save'; .save after a failed query is an
  error and writes nothing. A script can now tell 'ran, no rows' from
  'failed' by whether the file exists.
